\pard\ql\b\fs30 Website Introduction\b0\fs24\par\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa120\b\fs32 Welcome\b0\fs24\par\par
\pard\ql\li0\fi0 Welcome to your guide for choosing the best AI-tool for your needs. Discover a range of AI-tools designed to support both  teachers and students when it comes to languages. From creating pictures and assisting with writing to making a lesson plan. This website will assist you to find resources that enhance the efficiency of language learning.\par\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa120\b Advantages of AI in language education\b0\par\par
\pard\ql\li0\fi0 1. Enhanced learning outcomes > AI has the potential to transform language education by improving overall learning results. However, nuance is important: AI is most effective when used as a complementary tool alongside traditional teaching methods and human guidance, not on its own.\line                     2. Constant accessibility > AI tools are available 24/7, acting as an assistant to both teachers and students. It can be accessed both inside and outside the classroom.\line                     3. Workload reduction > Especially for teachers, AI tools can support them by taking over some time-consuming tasks, such as grading assignments or adapting texts to specific students    needs.\par\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa120\b Disadvantages of AI in language education\b0\par\par
\pard\ql\li0\fi0 1. Overreliance on AI > There are some consequences to consider when it comes to AI in education. A major issue is that students may become too dependent on AI tools, which can prevent them from engaging in the cognitive processes necessary to develop skills such as grammar. In addition, relying heavily on AI may reduce original thinking and creativity, eventually turning students into passive learners.\line                     2. Inaccurate Information > AI-tools are known to    hallucinate    from time to time, meaning they can show information that is not true. It   s important that students and teachers learn to critically evaluate when it comes to AI-generated content rather than trusting it unconditionally.\line                     3. Social Challenges > As of today, there is not enough research on the long-term effects of AI-tools in education, but there are worries that AI may reduce valuable interaction between teachers and students. Some believe that excessive use of AI could eventually affect students    social and emotional development.\par\par\page
